<task id="043" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Binder faults answer 503 and the SPA retries; ProjectPage 404 folded into 403 (FR-28, #2269)</title>
    <phase>4 Access, sign-in, carry-overs, Teams</phase>
    <gate>after 038 (P3 deploy); the ProjectPage fold also needs ebilling-r1's task-130 batch on master</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags bff-api and auth; modifies the caller-principal deny mapping (.cs) and the SPA sign-in path (.ts/.tsx)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Auth/access status mapping on the shared external plane (ADR-028: indeterminate → 503, never 403)</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>E</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>038</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, frontend, react, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make the caller-principal resolver answer a retryable 503 ProblemDetails (same reasonCode/errorCode, a retry message) when contact lookup, create or bind faults, keeping real denials at 403; make the SPA retry such a 503 three times (1 s, 2 s, 4 s) and then show "We couldn't finish signing you in. Try again" with a Retry button; fold ProjectPage's dead 404 branch into its 403 handling.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in the BFF's CallerPrincipalResolver deny mapping and the external SPA's /me client.</role>
  <goal>`contact_lookup_failed`, `contact_create_failed` and `contact_bind_failed` give 503 on both planes; not-invited and other denials stay 403; the SPA retries then shows the message with Retry and never a default workspace for these faults; ProjectPage has one 403 path; UAC's review is recorded.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>ADR-028: an indeterminate access result is a retryable 503, never a 403. Today the three binder fault codes (`ContactBindingDecision.DenyContactLookupFailed` :797, `DenyContactBindFailed` :842, `DenyContactCreateFailed` :851) fall into 403 in TWO places in CallerPrincipalResolver.cs: the workforce plane's default branch (:790-794, the spec's anchor) AND the CIAM plane's binder refusal (:514-524, `ProblemDetailsHelper.Forbidden(answer, ...)`). Precedent for the 503 shape: the invite routes already answer 503 `sdap.access.invite.contact_lookup_failed` (tests/integration/contract/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessContractTests.cs:822-860). SPA: me-client.ts `fetchMeEntitlements` (:144-175) degrades EVERY 5xx to the plane's default modules (:165-170) — a binder 503 must not do that. WorkforceHomeGate (header :18) maps 5xx to a generic retry state; BffAccessState `accessFailureOf` maps failures to states. ebilling-r1's task-130 batch (`work/ebilling-r1` 017a965312, 2026-11-10) makes a stale grant answer 403, not 404, so ProjectPage.tsx's 404 branch (:465-476) is dead once it is on master; the 403 branch is :451-463. The list `truncated` flag needs no change.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/api/me-client.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/components/auth/BffAccessState.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/components/auth/WorkforceHomeGate.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/pages/ProjectPage.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ContactBindingDecision.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Errors/ProblemDetailsHelper.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessContractTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolverTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new-artifact">tests/integration/auth/ExternalAccess/BinderFaultStatusTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new-artifact">src/client/external-spa/tests/me-client.binderFaultRetry.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="new-artifact">projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-043-notes.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="038" status="pending">P3 deployed and E2E-proved (phase-deploy convention)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 / spec FR-28">In CallerPrincipalResolver, exactly the three codes contact_lookup_failed, contact_create_failed and contact_bind_failed map to 503 on BOTH planes; every other deny code keeps its current status, body and detail (not-invited/removed stay the 403 not-invited answer; registration_required stays 403; owner-unconfigured stays 500).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">The 503 is ProblemDetails with the same `reasonCode` (and `errorCode`) value the 403 carried today, a fixed retry message as `detail`, and no exception text.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec FR-28">The SPA retries only a 503 whose reasonCode is one of the three binder codes: up to 3 retries at 1 s, 2 s, 4 s, then the fixed message "We couldn't finish signing you in. Try again" with a Retry button. It never shows a default workspace for these codes. Other 5xx keep today's behaviour.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec FR-28">Find and check every caller that reacts to these statuses (fetchMeEntitlements, getExternalUserContext/WorkforceHomeGate, BffAccessState, AuthGuard paths); list them with the decision per caller in the task notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project wave E">Do not edit tests/no-mock-identity.test.tsx (task 044 owns it in this wave): put new SPA tests in a new file. Do not edit widgetRegistry.ts (task 040).</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">Placement Justification in the PR (.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md); publish-size delta against a fresh master build, at or under 60 MB; no new HIGH CVE; tests with the change; /conflict-check before the PR (CallerPrincipalResolver.cs is shared with unified-access-control-r2 and ebilling-r1). Never deploy the dev BFF directly — request via uac-r2 (docs/procedures/dev-bff-deploy-coordination.md).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">Logs and errors carry no tenant, oid, UPN, email or token.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">BFF tests go under a KEEP path (tests/integration/auth/** or tests/integration/contract/**); no banned mocks (B1-B17); time in SPA retry tests via fake timers, not real delays.</constraint>
  </constraints>

