  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load the knowledge files, read the relevant files, declare rigor and model tier per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">Add the 503 branch for the three codes on the workforce plane (before the default at :790) and on the CIAM plane (:514-524); leave every other branch untouched.</step>
    <step order="2">BFF tests (KEEP path): each of the three codes → 503 with the same reasonCode on each plane; must-not-fire: contact_not_invited (and removed) → 403 unchanged; registration_required → 403 unchanged.</step>
    <step order="3">Seeding proof on the mapping: map one fault code back to 403, confirm its 503 test fails, restore; record it in the notes.</step>
    <step order="4">SPA: add the binder-503 retry (1/2/4 s, 3 retries) and the final message with Retry in the shared place the callers use; make fetchMeEntitlements skip the plane-default degrade for these codes; audit the other callers and record the list.</step>
    <step order="5">SPA tests (new file, fake timers): retry then success; retries exhausted then the message with a working Retry; a plain 503 without a binder code keeps today's behaviour; a 403 is not retried.</step>
    <step order="6">ProjectPage: once ebilling's task-130 batch is on master (check with `git merge-base --is-ancestor` or the merged PR), remove the 404 branch (:465-476) and let a 404 fall to the 403/denied handling; update tests/ProjectPage.*.test.tsx if they assert the 404 text.</step>
    <step order="7">Request UAC's review; record it in the notes and the PR.</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/`, the affected BFF tests, and the SPA tests; measure publish size per bff-extensions.</step>
    <step order="9">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` and this POML's &lt;status&gt; to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="10">Record deviations, decisions and measurements in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-043-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If ebilling's task-130 batch is not on master when the rest is done, ship without the ProjectPage fold, record it in the notes, and leave the fold as a named follow-up in this task's notes; do not fold early (the 404 is still live until then).</trigger>
    <trigger>If any caller cannot tell a binder 503 from another 5xx without a new response field, STOP and ask UAC before changing the response contract.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Binder fault retry then message">
      <url>https://{spa-dev-host}/</url>
      <steps>
        <step>With the BFF answering 503 contact_lookup_failed (test double or dev fault injection approved by the owner), sign in</step>
        <step>Watch the retries; after the last, check the message and click Retry</step>
        <step>Check the console: no token, email or oid printed</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Three retries, then "We couldn't finish signing you in. Try again" with a Retry button; no default workspace.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Message in dark mode (ADR-021)">
      <steps><step>Repeat with the dark theme</step></steps>
      <expected>Semantic tokens only; the message and button are legible.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

