  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Each of contact_lookup_failed, contact_create_failed and contact_bind_failed answers 503 ProblemDetails with the same reasonCode/errorCode and a retry message, on the workforce and the CIAM plane.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Must-not-fire: a not-invited (or removed) caller still gets the 403 not-invited answer; registration_required stays 403; owner-unconfigured stays 500.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The SPA retries a binder 503 three times at 1 s, 2 s and 4 s and succeeds when a retry succeeds (test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">After the retries are exhausted the SPA shows "We couldn't finish signing you in. Try again" with a Retry button that restarts the sequence (test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a binder 503 never yields the plane-default workspace; a 403 is never retried; a 5xx without a binder code behaves as before.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every caller of these statuses is listed in the notes with its handling.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ProjectPage has no 404-specific branch once ebilling's task-130 is on master (or the escalation is recorded).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The seeding proof is recorded; UAC's review is recorded in the notes and the PR.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build green; publish size at or under 60 MB with the delta against a fresh master build; no new HIGH CVE; /conflict-check run; all BFF and SPA tests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the must-not-fire and negative cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-28; issue #2269; NFR-07 must-fire/must-not-fire pair. Spec anchor drift: the spec cites only CallerPrincipalResolver.cs:790-794 (workforce); the CIAM plane's binder refusal at :514-524 also maps these codes to 403 and is in scope. Two adversarial-review passes (auth).</notes>

